%N A399342 Array read by ascending antidiagonals: A(n, k) = (1/k) * Sum_{j=0..n} A(n-j, k-1) * A(j, 1) * binomial(n+k, j+1) * binomial(n, j) for k >= 2, A(0, k) = 1, A(n, 0) = 0^n, and A(n, 1) = Sum_{j=1..n} j! * A(n-j, j).
%F A399342 If seen as a triangle, T(n, 1) = A398579(n) where we undersand T(0, 1) = 0.
%F A399342 T(n, k) * k! = A399444(n, k).
%e A399342 Seen as a triangle, T(n, k) = A(n-k, k), for k = 0..n:
